<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuroda Nagatomo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1839">1839</a>–<a href="/years/1902">1902</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kuroda Nagatomo was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukuoka">Fukuoka</a> domain, succeeding his adoptive father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuroda-nagahiro">Kuroda Nagahiro</a> in 1869. In 1870 domain officials were found counterfeiting money, and in 1871 he was dismissed as domain governor shortly before the domains were abolished. He later served the Meiji state, including as a diplomat and court official, and received the title of marquis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kuroda-nagatomo.jpg" alt="Kuroda Nagatomo" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 増原写真館撮影 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kuroda_Nagatomo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
